        "description": "## FFe ##\n\n[ Rationale ]\n* Merge target for stonking: 0.5.17-1ubuntu1, matching Debian unstable.\n* 0.5.16 fixes daily-driver bugs: Lua script crashes, monitor device\n  activation, default node selection, state handling. 0.5.17 fixes a\n  regression 0.5.16 introduced (object destruction via WpClientContext,\n  #999). Staying on 0.5.15 ships those bugs all cycle.\n* Delta stays minimal: only the snapd permission prompting module\n  (LP: #2144988), rediffed.\n\n[ Scope ]\n* Upstream 0.5.15 -> 0.5.17. Changelog diff attached. Highlights:\n  - WpClientContext: media objects (loopback, filter-chain, LocalNode,\n    SpaDevice) on a second PipeWire connection, so slow Lua hooks stop\n    stalling their control path. Export core retired.\n  - WpDynamicRules: matching rules with conditions. filter-graph graphs\n    load/unload dynamically.\n  - wpctl: new \"list\" and \"reset\" subcommands, \"--yes\" for reset.\n  - Bluetooth monitor rewritten on event hooks (#916).\n  - New WpPermissionManager and WpStateMetadata APIs.\n  - 0.5.17: fixed factory-created device/node/link ownership regression\n    (#999), default-nodes route ranking, better Lua POD errors.\n* Packaging:\n  - 10 new symbols in libwireplumber-0.5-0. SONAME unchanged, additive\n    only. No rdep rebuilds.\n  - New Build-Dep: libsnapd-glib-dev (>= 1.72), already in main.\n  - Allow lua5.5, matching Debian, now in main (LP: #2155757).\n* No reverse dependency builds against a changed ABI.\n\nseeded-in-ubuntu wireplumber:\nTODO(charles): seeded-in-ubuntu is currently returning 503's or hanging today.\nWill update when the infra is back.\n$ seeded-in-ubuntu wireplumber\nIssue fetching index file: HTTP Error 503: Service Unavailable\nMissing or empty index\n\n[ Regression Potential ]\n* WpClientContext moves media objects to a second connection and thread. If\n  wrong: devices or filters fail to appear, loopback and filter-chain link\n  failures, hangs on node creation. 0.5.17 already fixed the worst of it (#999).\n  This regression was the main reason 0.5.16 was not shipped.\n\n* Bluetooth monitor rewrite could break discovery or profile switching. Shows as\n  BT headsets missing or A2DP/HSP selection failing. Mitigation: I tested BT\n  profile switching on my local hardware.\n\n* Permission-manager refactor could grant or deny access wrongly. Shows as snap\n  apps losing mic access when Permission Prompting is enabled. Mitigation:\n  tested locally that Permission Prompting still works for Mic access.\n\n* Default-nodes ranking changes could pick the wrong device after reconnect.\n  Mitigation: didn't notice any regressions in behaviour during local testing.\n\n* snapd permission prompting module is Ubuntu-specific, no-op unless apparmor\n  prompting is enabled. Small blast radius.\n\n[ Testing ]\n* PPA: https://launchpad.net/~charles05/+archive/ubuntu/merge-wireplumber-lp2167863-stonking\n* Build: https://launchpad.net/~charles05/+archive/ubuntu/merge-wireplumber-lp2167863-stonking/+sourcepub/18747239/+listing-archive-extra\n* Installation:\n$ sudo apt install --reinstall wireplumber libwireplumber-0.5-0\nUpgrading:\n  libwireplumber-0.5-0  wireplumber\n\nSummary:\n  Upgrading: 2, Installing: 0, Removing: 0, Not Upgrading: 0\n  Download size: 0 B / 491 kB\n  Space needed: 57.3 kB / 27.4 GB available\n\n(Reading database… 458384 files and directories currently installed.)\nPreparing to unpack …/wireplumber_0.5.17-1ubuntu1~ppa1_amd64.deb…\nUnpacking wireplumber (0.5.17-1ubuntu1~ppa1) over (0.5.15-1ubuntu2)…\nPreparing to unpack …/libwireplumber-0.5-0_0.5.17-1ubuntu1~ppa1_amd64.deb…\nUnpacking libwireplumber-0.5-0:amd64 (0.5.17-1ubuntu1~ppa1) over (0.5.15-1ubuntu2)…\nSetting up libwireplumber-0.5-0:amd64 (0.5.17-1ubuntu1~ppa1)…\nSetting up wireplumber (0.5.17-1ubuntu1~ppa1)…\nProcessing triggers for libc-bin (2.44-1ubuntu1)…\n* Upgrade: from 0.5.15-1ubuntu2, config and state preserved.\n* Autopkgtest:\n  - amd64: https://autopkgtest.ubuntu.com/results/autopkgtest-stonking-charles05-merge-wireplumber-lp2167863-stonking/stonking/amd64/w/wireplumber/20260924_170834_f6965@/log.gz\n  - arm64: https://autopkgtest.ubuntu.com/results/autopkgtest-stonking-charles05-merge-wireplumber-lp2167863-stonking/stonking/arm64/w/wireplumber/20260924_170847_dcae8@/log.gz\n* Breaks other packages: no. No SONAME change, no rdep rebuilds.\n* Manual: device enumeration, default device switching, BT connect and\n  profile switch, filter-graph load, wpctl list/reset, snap audio\n  permission prompting.\n\n[ Other Info ]\n* Merge from Debian unstable. Delta reduced to the snapd patch plus\n  standard Ubuntu control changes.\n* FFE now avoids a bigger jump later in the cycle.",
